I used `__builtin_expect` to mark the rare `type`-valid and invalid-profile paths as cold, so the common profile-lookup path falls through and the cold returns are moved out of line, reducing taken branches and improving code layout.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(type != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 0))
        return type;

    const auto* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```